=== organization-people (head) ===
# Organization people roster

Effective project and repository account rosters are described in
[Resource people APIs](resource-people.md).

Core exposes two management-only organization reads:

- `GET /api/v1/orgs/{orgId}/people` returns a lightweight roster.
- `GET /api/v1/orgs/{orgId}/people/{accountId}/access` returns editing details for one person.

The roster always returns summaries. There is no `view` parameter or full-list mode.
Grant details and editing capabilities belong to the access endpoint only.

## Authorization and data boundaries

Both endpoints require authentication and `org#manage`, including the existing platform-admin fallback.
Ordinary members can still use `/members`. Repository `pull` permission is not required.

Both Core modes read global CockroachDB and global public identity data for people.
Neither endpoint reads regional private profiles.
Identity fields expose handles only for showable providers (currently GitHub).
They expose seed-once provider-asserted display names from global `public_profiles` and avatars.
They do not expose editable regional private display names or emails.
Non-showable providers retain `provider` and `accountId`, but their `handle` is omitted.
Each request checks organization existence and caller authorization before reading the roster.

The roster also reads outstanding invitations from the regional store.
So only the organization's home core serves the roster. Other cores answer 421.
The redirect runs after the manage check, so an unauthorized caller never learns the home core URL.
The redirect applies to every page and every filter.
The access endpoint reads only global data and does not redirect.
Invitation emails are regional PII. The roster includes them only when the caller passes the organization's SSO check.
A caller who fails that check still gets the people.

## Roster request

```http
GET /api/v1/orgs/{orgId}/people?scope=repository&search=alice&pageSize=50
```

All filters combine with AND and apply before counting and pagination:

| Parameter | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `search` | Trimmed, case-insensitive literal substring of account ID, any active public handle including provider prefix, or public display name. Maximum 200 characters. |
| `membership` | `member`: non-pending membership, including inactive; `invited`: WorkOS membership with status pending, not an email invitation; `collaborator`: no direct membership. |
| `status` | Direct membership status: `active`, `inactive`, or `pending`. Collaborators have no membership status. |
| `role` | Any recorded grant role: `owner`, `admin`, `member`, `reader`, `writer`, or `mirror_source_admin`. This includes weaker independent grants, not inherited roles. |
| `scope` | A recorded `organization`, `project`, or `repository` grant. This does not match inherited access. |
| `pageSize` | Default 50, capped at 200. Shared API validation accepts 0–500; 0 uses the default. |
| `pageToken` | Opaque account-ID keyset cursor from the previous page. |

Results sort by account ID, not display name. Keep filters unchanged while following a cursor.
Each page has one SQL snapshot. Concurrent changes can affect later pages.
A cursor never supplies scope or authorization.

