=== stale-read-metrics (head) ===
# Stale-read metrics

entire-core reads CockroachDB follower replicas and SpiceDB at minimized latency. A read right after a write can miss the write. Two counters show how often this happens and whether the fresh fallback catches it.

Use these counters with the [authorization caller policies](authorization-policy-callers.md) and the [CockroachDB read-locality ADR](../adrs/20260529-entire-core-crdb-read-locality.md).

## Metrics

Both counters live in `core/staleread`. Every label value comes from a fixed vocabulary in code. No label carries an ID.

| Metric | Labels | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `entire.core.stale_read.recheck.total` | `store`, `surface`, `outcome` | A fresh re-read of a stale miss or denial. |
| `entire.core.stale_read.pinned.total` | `store`, `surface` | A read served at a commit token or revision floor. |

`store` is `spicedb` or `crdb`.

### Outcomes

| `outcome` | Meaning | On-call reading |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `corrected` | The fresh answer differed from the stale one. A denial became an allow, or a miss became a hit. | The fix works. A nonzero rate is expected. |
| `confirmed` | The fresh answer agreed with the stale one. | Normal. A genuine denial or absence costs one extra read. |
| `fallback_failed` | The fresh read failed. A gate that confirms denials fails closed, and a `RetryDeniedFresh` batch keeps the stale denial. | A sustained rate means users see stale 403 and 404 responses again. Check SpiceDB and CockroachDB health first. |
| `canceled` | The caller ended the request during the fresh read. | Ignore, unless the rate tracks request latency. |

A CockroachDB follower error is not counted. The follower replica was unhealthy, so no stale answer existed. The store logs a warning for it.

### Surfaces

A SpiceDB surface is `<resource type>.<permission>`, such as `project.inspect` or `org.view`. A multi-action read pins under `<resource type>.bulk`.

Hand-written re-checks use these surfaces:

| Surface | Site |
| --- | --- |
| `project.inspect` | Project GET and project repository admission. |
| `project.resolve` | Project resolve by host and name. |
| `repo.pull_gate` | Repository GET pull gate. |
| `repo.public_access`, `repo_group.public_access` | Public wildcard checks. |

